.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.docker.example
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.superpowers/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Runtime data, credentials, recordings and generated reports.
# IoTGroup5/ is the live data directory (database + simulator token + backups):
# it sits inside the checkout for portability, so it must stay out of Git.
IoTGroup5/
data/**/*.db
data/**/*.sqlite*
data/**/*.wav
data/**/*.webm
data/**/*.mp3
data/**/*.mp4
data/secrets/
logs/
runtime/
reports/

# Generated reports and debug artifacts.
**/__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.pyc
acceptance-*.txt
*-report.txt

# Test code is kept locally and is deliberately not versioned: the suite exercises
# this machine's models, database and launcher scripts, and the repository ships
# without it. CI skips the test steps when the tree is absent (see ci.yml).
tests/

# Model artifacts are downloaded from the manifest, never committed.
models/**
!models/README.md
!models/manifest.json

# Third-party book corpora stay out of Git entirely: the sources are copyrighted (the first
# manual's PDF and its extracted Markdown were tracked until 2026-10-03 and have now been
# removed from the index too), and two of them are image-only scans from Anna's Archive /
# z-library. The files remain on disk, so the running knowledge base is unaffected; a fresh
# clone simply starts with an empty one and imports its own licensed corpus. Profiles and
# calibration sets ARE versioned (data/knowledge/), because they contain rules and questions,
# not book text. See docs/RAG_KNOWLEDGE_PLAN.md A9.7.7.
# The trailing '*' also covers archives of the corpus (e.g. data/RAG_data.rar, 55.5 MB, created
# 2026-10-05): the rule above matches the directory only, so a zipped copy next to it showed up as
# an ordinary untracked file and the next `git add -A` would have pushed the scans back into Git.
data/RAG_data/
data/RAG_data*

# Local editor and OS files.
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
# Agent tooling permissions. These files name absolute paths on the machine that wrote
# them, so they are machine-local by nature and must not travel with the checkout.
.claude/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# The PowerShell launchers under scripts/ ARE versioned: the .bat entrypoints
# call them, so ignoring them made a fresh clone unable to start. They resolve
# the interpreter through Resolve-ProjectPython instead of hardcoding one path.
